        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n`readResponseTextLimited` + raw body in error for Chutes token exchange and\nrefresh non-2xx responses. The body text was embedded in the Error message.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nReplaced with `extractProviderErrorDetail` for bounded, redacted structured\nerror detail. Removed now-unused `readResponseTextLimited` import and\n`CHUTES_OAUTH_ERROR_BODY_LIMIT_BYTES` constant. Follows #102953.\n\n## Evidence\n\n### Targeted path proof (Chutes OAuth via extractProviderErrorDetail)\n\nReal HTTP 400 with standard OAuth error body → `extractProviderErrorDetail(response)` in the exact exchangeChutesCodeForTokens/refreshChutesTokens pattern:\n\n```\n=== #103569 Proof: extractProviderErrorDetail on Chutes OAuth path ===\nStatus in message: PASS\nCode in detail (redacted): PASS\nSensitive text redacted: PASS\nRaw JSON keys not leaked: PASS\nStructured [code=...] format: PASS\nDetail bounded (65 chars): PASS\n\nMessage: Chutes token exchange failed with status 400: The access *** is invalid or has been revoked. [code=invalid_***]\nDetail: The access *** is invalid or has been revoked. [code=invalid_***]\n\nOverall: ALL PASS\n```\n\n### Import check\n\n`node --import tsx` — import OK\n\n### Diff\n\n```\nsrc/agents/chutes-oauth.ts | 16 ++++++-------\n```\n\n- [x] I understand what the code does\n- [x] Change is focused and does not mix unrelated concerns\n\n@clawsweeper re-review\n",
